#X obj 60 904 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 932 <pitch> <velocity> \, note <p> <v>: note on/off (0 = off) \; <p> <v> <channel>: from [notein] \, filtered by ch1 \; <control> <0-127>: set a control by name \, e.g. har1 64 \; ctl <index> <0-127> \, params v0 v1 ...: set by index \; <setting> <value>: e.g. cut 60 (see the settings blocks below) \; delay flanger / chorus1 / chorus2 / slap / long / off \; bend <-1..1>: pitch bend of all voices \, times bnd semitones \; n <name> <0-127>: a setting from a pot \, CV or MIDI CC \, \;   scaled to its range (switches in zones \, 64 = 0 if bipolar) \; nget <name> <tag>: outlet 3 gets norm <tag> <0-127> \, \;   the setting as a pot position (for pickup) \; ninfo <name>: outlet 3 gets info <name> <0-127> <value> \, \;   pot position and value with unit. Every change is also \;   reported this way by itself (editor \, controller layer) \; disp <name>: outlet 3 gets disp <label> <value> \, \;   two symbols for a display (OLED) \; oled <host> <port>: changed settings to O2O (an OLED) as \;   OSC \, sent from a thread of its own \; oledtext <line 1> <line 2>: two lines for the OLED \; defaults \, reset: default values \, reset also stops all voices \; panic: all voices off \; get <name>: reply 'value <name> <v>' on outlet 2 \; print: voices \, values and sample rate to the Pd window \; dump: send all values to outlet 2 as 'dump pdoly8 v0 ..' \; dump pdoly8 v0 v1 ...: restore such a dump (this voice only) \; voice <i> <p> \, voiceoff <i>: play one voice directly \; random <kind> [seed]: a new sound \, kind = pluck \, bass \, lead \, \;   brass \, pad \, strings or total (the MIDI channel stays) \; Poly-800 II sysex (the editor uses them): \; syxin <byte>: bytes from [sysexin] \, a whole data dump gives \;   bank <n> pdoly8 ... for the 64 programs on outlet 3 \; syxread <file> \, syxwrite <file>: a .syx file \; syxbank <n> pdoly8 ...: a preset into program n (0-63) \; syxsend: the dump as syxbyte <b> on outlet 3 (-> [midiout]) \;   needs a dump received or read first (sequencer \, chord \;   memory and MIDI channel are kept from it), f 64;
#X obj 60 1536 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Editor\ (p8edit) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1564 [p8edit \$0-pdoly8] above: click it to open the editor. All 115 settings in rows of 8: rows 1-11 are the CC pages of the controller layer \, then more and the own DEG stages. Each cell: name and CC number \, slider and number box 0-127 (the value as from a pot \, n <name> <value>) and the real value with its unit. \; It sends to the bus [s \$0-pdoly8] and reads outlet 3 from [s \$0-pdoly8-out]: pdoly8~ reports every change there (info) \, so the Launchkey \, presets and messages show up in it. In your own patch: [p8edit <name>] next to [r <name>] -> [pdoly8~] -> outlet 3 -> [s <name>-out]. \; Above the rows: factory presets \, MIDI channel \, the user bank (p8user-bank.txt next to the editor: store to N chooses the slot \, save patch stores and writes the file \, factory init) \, the delay presets \, random sounds (pluck \, bass \, lead \, brass \, pad \, strings \, total) and the Poly-800 II sysex. How it all works: [pd readme] inside the editor., f 64;
#X obj 60 1864 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MIDI\ CC:\ controller\ layer\ (p8cc) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1892 [p8cc 1] above is the controller layer of pdoly8~: MIDI CC on channel 1 (the argument \, 0 = all channels) -> n <name> <value> onto the bus. Every instrument gets its own channel and the same CC pages \, so the Launchkey keeps one setup: page k = row k in the editor. \; Pages: 20-119 without 32 \, 38 \, 64-69 \, 84 \, 88 \, 96-101 (bank / data LSB \, pedals \, portamento control \, high-res velocity \, NRPN / RPN). \; Changes from elsewhere (presets \, editor \, messages) go back to the controller as CC on the same channel and number. Pickup: after such a change an encoder acts only when it reaches the value or crosses it (pickup 0 turns that off). Inlet: outlet 3 of pdoly8~ (here [r \$0-pdoly8-out]) \, pickup 0/1 \, sync (send all values to the controller). CC 3 from the controller on the same channel does the same (the Launchkey firmware sends it before its first CC on a new channel). \; page 1 PLAY \, CC 20-27: har1 har2 env1 env2 intv detn lev1 lev2 \; page 2 FILTER \, CC 28-31 33-36: cut res egi env3 kbd vcut drv nois \; page 3 OSC \, CC 37 39-45: oct1 oct2 pw1 pw2 pwm1 pwm2 hmg drft \; page 4 WALSH-RING \, CC 46-53: wsh1 wsh2 wmx1 wmx2 wsm wse ring rmf \; page 5 SYNC-FM \, CC 54-61: sync swp2 swe swm fm1 fm2 fmr fmhz \; page 6 MG-FMSOURCE-DEG3 \, CC 62-63 70-75: mgr mgi mgd mgv fms fmig pol trg \; page 7 DELAY-EQ \, CC 76-83: dtim dfb dmf dmi dlev dgld treb bass \; page 8 PERFORM \, CC 85-87 89-93: port pmod mono retr vamp bnd sprd mrph \; page 9 DEG4-DRIVE \, CC 94-95 102-107: env4 trg4 d4t1 d4a1 d4t2 d4a2 drvp tone \; page 10 LFO2 \, CC 108-115: l2r l2w l2k l2f l2t1 l2a1 l2t2 l2a2 \; page 11 LFO3 \, CC 116-119: l3r l3w l3t1 l3a1 \; Every continuous setting is smoothed over mrph ms (25) \, so CC steps become ramps., f 64;
#X obj 60 2480 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls\ (index\ name\ default) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2508 0 har1 (45): Timbre of DCO1 \, one knob through all 15 distinct original timbres \, dark to bright: 0 16' / 9-64 saw net (16'2' \, 16'4'2' \, 16'4' \, 16'8'4' \, all at 45 \, 16'8'2' \, 16'8') / 73-127 square net (16'8' \, 16'8'4' \, 16'4' \, 16'4'2' \, all \, 16'8'2' \, 16'2'). One foot or the net per step \, no jumps. Combinations without 16' = oct1 2-4. \; 1 har2 (45): Timbre of DCO2 \, same path. \; 2 env1 (0): Envelope of DCO1 (DEG1) \, one knob: 0 gate / 1 very short pluck (no fade from the gate) / 24 pluck / 48 piano / 72 long release / 92 swell / 108 pad / 127 long pad. -1 = own values a1 ... r1. \; 3 env2 (0): Envelope of DCO2 (DEG2) \, the same \, -1 = own values a2 ... r2. \; 4 intv (0): Interval of DCO2 above DCO1 in semitones \, 0-12 \, as stored on the Poly-800 II. \; 5 detn (0): Detune of DCO2 downwards: the original's 4 steps 0 \, 6.5 \, 13 \, 26 cents lie at 0 \, 42 \, 85 \, 127. \; 6 lev1 (127): Level of DCO1. \; 7 lev2 (0): Level of DCO2 (every voice has both DCOs). Above full scale (lev1 + lev2 > 127) both are scaled down together., f 64;
#X obj 60 2856 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Timbre\ (har1\ /\ har2) 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2884 The 15 distinct timbres of the original \, dark to bright: \; 0: 16' / saw net 9: 16'2' / 18: 16'4'2' / 27: 16'4' / \; 36: 16'8'4' / 45: all / 54: 16'8'2' / 64: 16'8' / \; square net 73: 16'8' / 82: 16'8'4' / 91: 16'4' / \; 100: 16'4'2' / 109: all / 118: 16'8'2' / 127: 16'2'. \; One foot or the net per step. The combinations without 16' \; are the same waves higher: use oct1 / oct2 2-4. \; A fading foot rises in power \, so the morph has no dips., f 64;
#X obj 60 3040 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3068 Two read-only lists send presets to the object \, changing \; slots never writes anything back. Both send 'dump pdoly8 ...' \; messages (here via [s] \, nothing is wired across the patch). \; [p8factory]: the 64 Poly-800 II factory programs \, slot 0-63 \; (0 = program 11 \, 7 = 18 \, 8 = 21 ... 63 = 88) \, read from \; presets/poly800mk2-factory.txt next to the abstraction. \; [p8user name]: your own sounds in a [text define -k name] \; (saved with the patch). A slot number recalls \, only \; 'store N' writes: it stores the current sound in slot N \; (it needs outlet 2 of pdoly8~ at its right inlet \, here \; via [s]/[r]). 'write file' / 'read file' on the text \; define save and load banks. tools/p8sysex.py converts \; Poly-800 II sysex dumps to preset text and back., f 64;
