#X obj 252 3424 text define -k \$0-mine;
#X obj 60 3481 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty DCO\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3509 Settings: har1 har2 hmg / oct1 oct2 / pw1 pw2 pwm1 pwm2 / wsh1 wsh2 wmx1 wmx2 / wsm wse / sync swp2 swe swm / ring rmf - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 3615 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 3585 pw1 30;
#X msg 232 3585 sync 1 \, swe 50;
#X msg 382 3585 ring 100;
#X text 82 3658 Timbre \, octave and the modulations of the tone generators. Beyond har and oct nothing here is on the Poly-800. All edges stay band-limited. In this order: timbre \, octave \, PWM \, Walsh loop \, sync \, ring. \; har1 \, har2 (45): timbre of DCO1 / DCO2 \, the same as the controls above (see Timbre). \; hmg (0): the MG moves har1 and har2 by +-hmg steps \, 127 = through the whole timbre path (rate mgr / mgf \, delay mgd). \; oct1 \, oct2 (0): -1 0 1 = LOW MID HIGH \, 2-4: the feet one to three octaves higher (the combinations without 16'). \; pw1 \, pw2 (64): pulse width 0-127 = 3-97 % \, 64 = square. Every foot becomes the AND of itself and a copy shifted by part of its period (pulse staircases on the saw net). \; pwm1 \, pwm2 (0): the MG moves the width \, 127 = +-47 %. \; Walsh loop: the four feet are square waves of one counter \, an octave apart. Multiplying them (XOR of the counter bits) gives 15 Walsh functions \, square-like waves with 1 to 8 cycles per 16' period (sequency) and their energy near that harmonic. They come from the same counter edges \, so they are exactly in tune and band-limited - a wavetable the chip already has. The loop orders them by sequency: moving along it sweeps the energy from the 16' up to the 8th harmonic and back \, neighbours fading at equal power. \; wsh1 \, wsh2 (0): position on the loop 0-127 (0: 16' / 17: 16'x4' / 59: 2' / 85: all four / 119: 16'x8' / 127 = 0 again). \; wmx1 \, wmx2 (0): mix from the normal feet (0) to the loop (127). \; wsm (0): the MG moves the position +-wsm steps (127: the whole loop \, a sweeping \, vocal sound - try mgr 2-8). \; wse (0): DEG3 moves the position by up to wse steps (-127..127) \, e.g. a bright attack falling into the 16'. wsm and wse act where wmx is above 0. \; sync (0): 1: DCO2's counter restarts at every 16' period of DCO1 \, at the exact sub-sample time. \; swp2 (0): DCO2 offset 0-72 semitones. \; swe (0): DEG3 adds up to 0-72 semitones to DCO2. \; swm (0): the MG adds +-0-24 semitones to DCO2. Screaming sync: sync 1 \, lev1 low \, lev2 high \, swe 40-72 \, a falling DEG3 (d3 \, su3 0) \, res and drv up. The sweeps also work without sync. \; ring (0): 0-127 \, DCO2 is multiplied by a +-1 wave of DCO1 (XOR \, the ring modulation of square waves). At 127 only sum and difference tones remain \, lev1 0 for the pure ring sound. \; rmf (0): the modulator \, a step 0-14 on the Walsh loop of DCO1: 0 its 16' (softest) \, 1 8' \, 3 4' \, 7 2' \, 10 all four feet \, back down to 14 16'x8'. Steps towards 7 move the sidebands further apart: stronger \, more metallic., f 64;
#X obj 60 4422 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty FM 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4450 Settings: fm1 fm2 / fms fmr fmhz fmig - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 4540 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 4510 fm1 60;
#X msg 232 4510 fmr 2;
#X msg 382 4510 fms 1;
#X floatatom 82 4572 6 0 0 0 - - -;
#X obj 82 4602 osc~ 110;
#X obj 82 4632 s~ \$0-fmin;
#X text 172 4602 external modulator (fms 2);
#X text 82 4675 Linear FM of the counter rate \, through zero (the counter runs backwards) above index 1 \, every edge band-limited. Not on the Poly-800. \; fm1 \, fm2 (0): depth on DCO1 / DCO2 \, 0-127 = index 0-16 (1 at about 32) \, 0 = off. \; fms (0): chooses the modulator \, it switches nothing on or off: 0 a sine per DCO at fmr x its own 16' frequency plus fmhz \, 1 the other DCO of the voice (cross FM: DCO2 into DCO1 and DCO1 into DCO2) \, 2 the signal at the right inlet (about -1..1: osc~ \, adc~ \, noise~ ...) \, here from the osc~ above. \; fmr (1): 0.125-16 \, whole ratios stay harmonic \, others (1.41 \, 3.5) give bells and metal that follow the key. From a pot \, CC or the editor in harmonic steps (1/8 1/4 1/3 1/2 2/3 3/4 1 5/4 4/3 3/2 2 5/2 3 7/2 4-16) \, so 1 is always found again. Inharmonic: fmhz \, or any ratio as a message (fmr 1.41). \; fmhz (0): -1000..1000 Hz added to the sine: a fixed \, inharmonic offset with the same beat on every key (fmr 0.125 \, fmhz 200: almost a fixed modulator). \; fmig (64): gain of the signal at the right inlet (fms 2) \, 64 = 1 \, 127 = about 2., f 64;
#X obj 60 5023 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Filter\ &\ DEG3\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5051 Settings: cut res kbd / egi pol trg / env3 / a3 d3 bp3 sl3 su3 r3 / nois / drv drvp / vcut - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 5157 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 5127 cut 40;
#X msg 232 5127 res 12;
#X msg 382 5127 drv 80;
#X text 82 5200 One 4-pole VCF for the instrument (NJM2069) and one DEG3 for all voices \, measured on a Poly-800 II. \; cut (99): 0-99 = 66 Hz - 20 kHz \, 13 steps per octave. \; res (0): 0-15 \, an uncompensated ladder (the bass falls as it rises) \, no self-oscillation. \; kbd (0): key tracking of the highest key: 0 off \, 2 full (1:1 \, C4 nominal) \, 1 half (1:2 \, C6 nominal). \; egi (0): EG INT 0-15 \, DEG3 moves the cutoff up to 7.9 octaves. \; pol (2): 2 up \, 1 down. \; trg (2): 2 multi: every key restarts DEG3 \, 1 single: only the first key of a phrase. \; env3 (0): DEG3 morph as env1 (see Controls) \, -1 = own values. \; a3 d3 bp3 sl3 su3 r3: attack \, decay \, break point \, slope \, sustain \, release of DEG3 \, 0-31. \; nois (0): white noise 0-15 \, its VCA follows DEG3. \; drv (0): overdrive (not on the Poly-800) \, soft clipping \, 0-127 = 0-48 dB more gain with level makeup. \; drvp (0): 0 post: after the VCF \, denser with res and chords \, 1 pre: into the VCF \, which rounds the distortion off (warmer). \; vcut (0): velocity to the cutoff: at 127 a soft key is up to 5 octaves lower \, full velocity plays the cut set (one VCF: the last key counts)., f 64;
#X obj 60 5580 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty MG\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5608 Settings: mgr mgf / mgi mgd / mgv - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 5698 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 5668 mgr 8;
#X msg 232 5668 mgi 50;
#X msg 382 5668 mgv 5;
#X text 82 5741 One triangle MG for the instrument \, measured on a Poly-800 II. It also drives hmg \, pwm1/2 \, wsm and swm (DCO settings). More LFOs: LFO2 and LFO3 below. \; mgr (-1): frequency in steps 0-15 as parameter 81 (0: 0.29 Hz / 3: 1.26 / 8: 5.2 / 15: 19 Hz) \, sets mgf. -1 = use mgf. \; mgf (5): the same in Hz. \; mgi (0): depth on the pitch in cents (83: 12.4 cents per step \, 186 at 15) \, a 14.5 Hz low-pass makes fast vibrato shallower \, as on the original. \; mgd (0): delay 0-15 (82: 0.47 s at 5 \, 1.55 s at 15) from the first key \, then full depth. \; mgv (0): MG to the VCF 0-15 (84: +-7.9 octaves at 15)., f 64;
#X obj 60 5961 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty DEG4\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5989 Settings: env4 trg4 / a4 d4 bp4 sl4 su4 r4 / d4t1 d4a1 d4t2 d4a2 - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 6095 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 6065 d4t1 cut \, d4a1 90;
#X msg 232 6065 d4t1 swe \, d4a1 70;
#X msg 382 6065 d4t1 fm1 \, d4a1 100;
#X text 82 6138 A modulation envelope (not on the Poly-800) \, one for all voices like DEG3. The Poly-800 is paraphonic: every voice has its own DEG1 / DEG2 \, but the VCF \, DEG3 and the MG exist once - and so do DEG4 \, LFO2 and LFO3. Each of them has two target slots: t = target (number or name \, e.g. d4t1 cut) \, a = amount -127..127 (negative inverts). \; env4 (0): DEG4 morph as env1 (see Controls) \, -1 = own values. \; trg4 (2): 2 multi: every key restarts DEG4 \, 1 single: only the first key of a phrase. \; a4 d4 bp4 sl4 su4 r4: attack \, decay \, break point \, slope \, sustain \, release of DEG4 \, 0-31. DEG4 runs 0..1 (its level \, linear). \; d4t1 \, d4a1 \, d4t2 \, d4a2: two targets and amounts. E.g. cut with a pluck (filter sweep per key) \, swe with sync 1 (sync sweep) \, fm1 (FM that decays) \, l2d (an LFO2 that comes in). \;   \; Targets (number name: parameter \, range at amount 127): \; 0 off: no target \; 1 pitch: pitch \, both DCOs +-24 semitones \; 2 pitch2: pitch DCO2 +-48 semitones \; 3 detn: detune DCO2 +-50 cents \; 4 har1: timbre DCO1 +-127 steps \; 5 har2: timbre DCO2 +-127 steps \; 6 wsh1: Walsh position DCO1 +-127 steps \; 7 wsh2: Walsh position DCO2 +-127 steps \; 8 wmx1: Walsh mix DCO1 +-127 \; 9 wmx2: Walsh mix DCO2 +-127 \; 10 pw1: pulse width DCO1 +-47 % \; 11 pw2: pulse width DCO2 +-47 % \; 12 fm1: FM depth DCO1 +-16 index \; 13 fm2: FM depth DCO2 +-16 index \; 14 fmr: FM ratio x/: 4 \; 15 ring: ring modulation amount +-127 \; 16 swe: sync sweep depth +-72 semitones \; 17 lev1: level DCO1 +-127 \; 18 lev2: level DCO2 +-127 \; 19 amp: output level x 0..2 (tremolo) \; 20 pan: balance left / right \; 21 nois: noise level +-15 \; 22 cut: cutoff filter +-8 octaves \; 23 res: resonance filter +-15 \; 24 drv: overdrive +-127 \; 25 mgr: MG rate x/: 8 \; 26 mgi: MG pitch depth +-200 cents \; 27 l2r: LFO2 rate x/: 8 \; 28 l2d: LFO2 depth x 0..2 \; 29 l3r: LFO3 rate x/: 8 \; 30 l3d: LFO3 depth x 0..2 \; 31 dtim: delay time x/: 2 \; 32 dlev: delay level +-15 \; har \, wsh \, wmx \, lev \, detn and drv follow per audio block (smoothed by mrph) \, all others per sample., f 64;
#X obj 60 6998 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty LFO2\ &\ LFO3\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 7026 Settings: l2r l2w l2k l2f / l2t1 l2a1 l2t2 l2a2 / l3r l3w l3k l3f / l3t1 l3a1 l3t2 l3a2 - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 7132 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 7102 l2t1 pitch \, l2a1 20;
#X msg 232 7102 l2t1 har1 \, l2a1 90;
#X msg 382 7102 l3t1 cut \, l3a1 60;
#X text 82 7175 Two more LFOs (not on the Poly-800) \, one each for all voices \, output -1..1. \; l2r \, l3r (2): rate 0.01-50 Hz. \; l2w \, l3w (0): wave 0 triangle \, 1 sine \, 2 saw up \, 3 saw down \, 4 square \, 5 sample & hold (a new random value each cycle). \; l2k \, l3k (0): retrigger: 0 free running \, 1 every key restarts the wave \, 2 only the first key of a phrase. \; l2f \, l3f (0): fade-in after a retrigger \, 0-10 s. \; l2t1 \, l2a1 \, l2t2 \, l2a2: two targets and amounts of LFO2. \; l3t1 \, l3a1 \, l3t2 \, l3a2: the same for LFO3. \;   \; Targets (number name: parameter \, range at amount 127): \; 0 off: no target \; 1 pitch: pitch \, both DCOs +-24 semitones \; 2 pitch2: pitch DCO2 +-48 semitones \; 3 detn: detune DCO2 +-50 cents \; 4 har1: timbre DCO1 +-127 steps \; 5 har2: timbre DCO2 +-127 steps \; 6 wsh1: Walsh position DCO1 +-127 steps \; 7 wsh2: Walsh position DCO2 +-127 steps \; 8 wmx1: Walsh mix DCO1 +-127 \; 9 wmx2: Walsh mix DCO2 +-127 \; 10 pw1: pulse width DCO1 +-47 % \; 11 pw2: pulse width DCO2 +-47 % \; 12 fm1: FM depth DCO1 +-16 index \; 13 fm2: FM depth DCO2 +-16 index \; 14 fmr: FM ratio x/: 4 \; 15 ring: ring modulation amount +-127 \; 16 swe: sync sweep depth +-72 semitones \; 17 lev1: level DCO1 +-127 \; 18 lev2: level DCO2 +-127 \; 19 amp: output level x 0..2 (tremolo) \; 20 pan: balance left / right \; 21 nois: noise level +-15 \; 22 cut: cutoff filter +-8 octaves \; 23 res: resonance filter +-15 \; 24 drv: overdrive +-127 \; 25 mgr: MG rate x/: 8 \; 26 mgi: MG pitch depth +-200 cents \; 27 l2r: LFO2 rate x/: 8 \; 28 l2d: LFO2 depth x 0..2 \; 29 l3r: LFO3 rate x/: 8 \; 30 l3d: LFO3 depth x 0..2 \; 31 dtim: delay time x/: 2 \; 32 dlev: delay level +-15 \; har \, wsh \, wmx \, lev \, detn and drv follow per audio block (smoothed by mrph) \, all others per sample., f 64;
#X obj 60 7955 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Delay\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 7983 Settings: dtim dfb / dmf dmi / dlev dgld - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 8103 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 8043 delay flanger;
#X msg 232 8043 delay chorus1;
#X msg 382 8043 delay chorus2;
