#X msg 232 8073 delay long;
#X msg 382 8073 delay off;
#X text 82 8146 The digital delay of the Poly-800 II (71-75) \, measured: the echo is in phase on the left output and inverted on the right (a mono sum cancels it). A gate ends the echo train \, changing a value mutes the echo for a moment \, as on the original. \; dtim (30): 0-99 = 4.2 ms - 1.08 s (70: 216 ms). \; dfb (0): feedback 0-15 (15: -3.1 dB per echo). \; dmf (0): mod rate 0-31 = 0.05-5 Hz. \; dmi (0): mod depth 0-31 (31: the time swings 1:5 \, about 10 dB less per 10 steps below). \; dlev (0): echo level 0-15 \, 0 = off. \; dgld (1): 1: changes glide (time like a tape \, feedback and level smoothed) \, for MIDI CC and modulation \, 0: every change mutes the echo for 40 ms \, as on the original. \; Presets: flanger (4 ms \, slow sweep \, feedback) \, chorus1 (fast \, shallow) \, chorus2 (slow \, wider) \, slap (120 ms) \, long (0.5 s with repeats) \, off., f 64;
#X obj 60 8430 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty DEG1\ &\ DEG2\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 8458 Settings: a1 d1 bp1 sl1 su1 r1 / a2 d2 bp2 sl2 su2 r2 / vamp - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 8564 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 8534 env1 24;
#X msg 232 8534 env1 108;
#X msg 382 8534 vamp 100;
#X text 82 8607 Each voice's DCO1 and DCO2 have their own 6-stage DEG as on the Poly-800. Measured on a Poly-800 II: level 0-31 is about (L/31)^2 \, attack rises linearly (31: about 9 s) \, decay \, slope and release fall at a constant dB per second (31: about 18 s to -40 dB). env1 / env2 (Controls) morph through: 0 gate / 1 short pluck / 24 pluck / 48 piano / 72 long release / 92 swell / 108 pad / 127 long pad. \; a1 d1 bp1 sl1 su1 r1: attack \, decay \, break point \, slope \, sustain \, release of DEG1 (DCO1) \, 0-31. Setting one makes env1 -1. \; a2 d2 bp2 sl2 su2 r2: the same for DEG2 (DCO2) \, env2 -1. \; vamp (0): velocity to the level of each voice (both DCOs \, not on the Poly-800): 0 off \, 127 level = velocity., f 64;
#X obj 60 8843 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Portamento 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 8871 Settings: port pmod / mono retr - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 8961 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 8931 port 60;
#X msg 232 8931 mono 1;
#X msg 382 8931 pmod 2;
#X text 82 9004 Not on the Poly-800. \; port (0): glide time 0-127 = off to 3 s. \; pmod (0): where a glide starts: 0 from the last note played \, 1 from the note this voice played before \, 2 from the last note only while another key is still held (legato glide). pmod is not a mono / poly switch. \; mono (0): 0 poly (4 voices) \, 1 mono: one voice \, the last key wins. \; retr (1): in mono \, 1: every key restarts the envelopes \, 0: legato \, only the first key of a phrase restarts them \, further keys (and going back to a held one) only change the pitch., f 64;
#X obj 60 9208 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Additional\ settings 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 9236 Settings: bnd ch1 / treb bass / sprd mrph / tone leak / drft - all of them in the editor (p8edit) \, as messages: <name> <value>., f 64;
#X obj 412 9342 s \$0-pdoly8;
#X msg 82 9312 bnd 12;
#X msg 232 9312 sprd 100;
#X msg 382 9312 drft 60;
#X text 82 9385 bnd (2): bend range in semitones (original: up to 7). Pitch bend from a MIDI keyboard comes in through [bendin] at the top. \; ch1 (1): MIDI channel for p v ch lists and for the controller layer \, 0 = any. It belongs to the setup: defaults and presets keep it (set it here or with MIDI ch in the editor). \; treb \, bass (0): EQ -6..6 (76/77 \, measured: about 4 dB at 3 \, 10 dB at 6 \, shelves at 4.3 kHz and 115 Hz). \; sprd (0): stereo spread of the 4 voices 0-127. \; mrph (25): smoothing time in ms of every continuous setting (timbre \, levels \, cutoff \, resonance \, FM \, ring \, drive \, noise \, DCO2 pitch \, detune \, vibrato \, EG depth ...) \, so MIDI CC steps become ramps. 0 = none. \; tone (1): 1: output stage measured on a Poly-800 (54 Hz high-pass \, VCF \, 1 pole at 5 kHz) \, 0: raw tone generators. \; leak (0): 1: released voices stay at -55 dB \, as on the original. \; drft (0): analogue drift (not on the Poly-800 \, whose pitch comes from a crystal and dividers) \, like the slop / vintage knob of newer Sequential instruments: every DCO of every voice wanders slowly and on its own (at 127 about +-3 cents \, peaks about 8) \, each note's envelopes run a little faster or slower (+-20 % \, DEG3 too) \, the MG rate wanders +-10 % and the cutoff +-0.2 octaves. 0 = exact., f 64;
#X text 82 9797 Credits: Modelled on the Korg Poly-800 service manual \, \; MSM5232 \, scale ROM data as documented in MAME's \; msm5232.cpp with help by Claude, f 64;
